; -----------------------------------------------------------------------
; Calibration, imported from "Octet - Calibration.dc.html"
; (docs/DESIGN_HANDOFF.md). Colours baked as literal DesignTokens values --
; .tscn parses before autoloads exist, same documented exception as
; game/gameplay.tscn:
;   COLOR_INK             #0C0A0F -> Color(0.047, 0.039, 0.059, 1)
;   COLOR_SURFACE         #16131B -> Color(0.086275, 0.07451, 0.105882, 1)
;   COLOR_SURFACE_RAISED  #1F1A26 -> Color(0.121569, 0.101961, 0.14902, 1)
;   COLOR_HAIRLINE        #2A2431 -> Color(0.164706, 0.141176, 0.192157, 1)
;   COLOR_TEXT_PRIMARY    #F5F1F5 -> Color(0.960784, 0.945098, 0.960784, 1)
;   COLOR_TEXT_SECONDARY  #A79FAE -> Color(0.654902, 0.623529, 0.682353, 1)
;   COLOR_TEXT_MUTED      #6E6676 -> Color(0.431373, 0.4, 0.462745, 1)
;   COLOR_PINK            #FF2D6E -> Color(1, 0.176471, 0.431373, 1)
;   COLOR_AMBER           #FFC93C -> Color(1, 0.788235, 0.235294, 1)
;
; Fidelity-pass note (CLAUDE.md design-fidelity rule): the mockup's ring
; pulse/top-tick animation runs on a fixed CSS loop independent of the
; sample "120 BPM" shown; here it's driven by the real beat instead (see
; calibration.gd's _flash_pulse), which reads truer than mimicking a fixed
; period unrelated to the actual metronome tempo. The mockup's sample
; "AUDIO OFFSET -18ms" is not faked -- audio_offset_ms is shown as whatever
; SettingsStore already has (0 by default; this routine only ever writes
; input_offset_ms, per the documented confounded-measurement decision
; below in calibration.gd).
; -----------------------------------------------------------------------

